From 0a02e5cc828c74a3a330959a5771a7c71cf36b5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:33:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sd: Keep the card when the extension registers cannot be
 read

mmc_sd_init_card() drops the card when sd_read_ext_regs() fails. The
extension registers are optional: sd_read_ext_regs() already returns 0
for a layout it does not support, and the card works without the
features they describe (power management and performance extensions).

A CRC error on the CMD48 read right after tuning makes the whole init
fail. The card then stays missing until it is reinserted, as the core
does not retry the init.

Warn and continue without the extensions instead.

Reported-by: vitalo233 <vitalo233@gmail.com>
Closes: https://github.com/joonhoekim/tb323fu-linux/issues/26
Suggested-by: vitalo233 <vitalo233@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/core/sd.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/core/sd.c b/drivers/mmc/core/sd.c
index c763efb10f..26c6d432e4 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/sd.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/sd.c
@@ -1563,8 +1563,11 @@ static int mmc_sd_init_card(struct mmc_host *host, u32 ocr,
 	if (!oldcard) {
 		/* Read/parse the extension registers. */
 		err = sd_read_ext_regs(card);
-		if (err)
-			goto free_card;
+		if (err) {
+			pr_warn("%s: error %d reading SD ext regs, ignoring them\n",
+				mmc_hostname(host), err);
+			err = 0;
+		}
 	}
 
 	/* Enable internal SD cache if supported. */
-- 
2.43.0

